WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
In June 2022, US consumer
prices were 9.1 percent

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.960
higher than a year before.

3
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.010
That was the largest
12-month rise since 1981.

4
00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.660
Now picture getting a raise of 30 percent.

5
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.690
Sounds great. But if
prices climbed faster,

6
00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.270
your paycheck buys less than before.

7
00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.820
So how can one number tell you how much

8
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:25.090
prices have risen for a
whole country of shoppers?

9
00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:28.260
In this mission, you'll build
a price index from scratch

10
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.460
and calculate the inflation rate.

11
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:33.570
Then you'll turn nominal
dollars into real ones,

12
00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:36.540
and see why the official
measure can mislead.

13
00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.770
Your mission: find out
how inflation is measured,

14
00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:41.720
and how far to trust the number.
